      "correction": "Each run derives one identity; the compose project and the run root under artifacts/run-output are both derived from it.",
      "proof": "Two runs started at the same moment against different brokers: both exit zero, distinct identities, distinct roots, zero containers left. A run killed while its fixture was up leaves exactly one container named after its own project and touches nothing else."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Generators write where their caller points them.",
      "detail": "change_list.py, freeze_manifest.py, artifact_gate.py and the other identity gates take an explicit target or a --repository root. They mutate nothing that was not named on the command line, which is why the ChangeList tests could be isolated by giving them their own repository rather than by changing the generator.",
      "correction": "none needed"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The diagnostics write only to --output or to standard output.",
